apt 2.7.14 cmake: use GNUTLS_INCLUDE_DIRS (plural) in methods target

CMake's built-in FindGnuTLS module sets the variables
GNUTLS_INCLUDE_DIRS and GNUTLS_LIBRARIES (plural).  methods/CMakeLists.txt
however referenced the singular form ${GNUTLS_INCLUDE_DIR}, which is never
defined, so target_include_directories(connectlib ...) received an empty
list and the compile of methods/connect.cc failed with:

  methods/connect.cc:23:10: fatal error: 'gnutls/gnutls.h' file not found

On a distro Linux build /usr/include happens to hold gnutls/gnutls.h, so
the empty include list is harmless and the bug is invisible.  On a cross
build (OHOS) the conan prefix include dir is only reachable through
GNUTLS_INCLUDE_DIRS and the build fails.

Fix by using the plural variable, matching what CMake's FindGnuTLS
actually exports.
--- a/methods/CMakeLists.txt
+++ b/methods/CMakeLists.txt
@@ -17,7 +17,7 @@
 
 if (HAVE_GNUTLS)
   target_compile_definitions(connectlib PRIVATE ${GNUTLS_DEFINITIONS})
-  target_include_directories(connectlib PRIVATE ${GNUTLS_INCLUDE_DIR})
+  target_include_directories(connectlib PRIVATE ${GNUTLS_INCLUDE_DIRS})
 endif()
 target_include_directories(http PRIVATE $<$<BOOL:${SYSTEMD_FOUND}>:${SYSTEMD_INCLUDE_DIRS}>)
 

